  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 1140 PM CDT TUE SEP 15 2026\n\nA ridge centered near Tennessee will dominate the regional\nweather pattern over the next few days. This persistent upper-\nlevel feature will keep rain chances under 15% while driving high\ntemperatures into the low-to-upper 90s through the end of the\nweek, approaching near-record daily highs in locations such as\nBirmingham and Montgomery. Lower dew points within this drier\nairmass should keep peak heat index values between 101 and\n104 degrees, remaining just below heat advisory thresholds.\n\nBy this weekend and into next week, the pattern begins to\ntransition as an upper-level low tracks west around the periphery\nof the ridge near Florida, alongside a weak surface trough/front\nmoving over the Midwest. The influx of returning Gulf moisture\nwill weaken the ridge and support a modest uptick in scattered\nafternoon and early evening shower and thunderstorm chances\nstarting Sunday and continuing into early next week, as well as\nslightly tempering the hot temperatures. However, unless the\nprojected pattern shifts significantly, widespread drought relief\nis unlikely.\n\n16",
